:: School Discipline Widgets [widget]
/* Status line shown in the front courtyard while a suspension is being served. */
<<widget "schoolDisciplineStatus">>
	<<run ensureSchoolDiscipline()>>
	<<if $schoolDiscipline.suspended is 1>>
		<span class="red">You're suspended.</span>
		<<if $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone gte $schoolDiscipline.serviceRequired>>
			You've served every session the school asked for.
			<<if $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft gt 0>>
				<span class="blue">There are still <<print $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft>> day<<if $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft isnot 1>>s<</if>> left on the suspension itself.</span>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="blue">Community service: <<print $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone>> of <<print $schoolDiscipline.serviceRequired>> sessions done.</span>
			<<if $schoolDiscipline.serviceMissed gt 0>>
				<span class="red">You've skipped <<print $schoolDiscipline.serviceMissed>>.</span>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* Links the courtyard offers a suspended PC: the service muster, and the readmission meeting. */
<<widget "schoolDisciplineOptions">>
	<<run ensureSchoolDiscipline()>>
	<<if $schoolDiscipline.suspended is 1>>
		<<if schoolReadmissionDue() and Time.schoolDay and Time.hour gte 8 and Time.hour lte 15>>
			<<schoolicon "headdesk">><<link [[See the head about coming back|School Readmission]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<elseif schoolServiceAvailable()>>
			<<if $exposed gte 1>>
				<span class="blue">You can't report for community service while you're this exposed.</span>
				<br>
			<<else>>
				<<schoolicon "courtyard">><<link [[Report for community service|School Service Report]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<<elseif $schoolDiscipline.servedToday is 1>>
			<span class="blue">You've done your service for today.</span>
			<br>
		<<elseif $schoolDiscipline.leftToday is 1>>
			<span class="red">You walked out on today's session. The van has gone.</span>
			<br>
		<<elseif schoolReadmissionDue()>>
			<span class="blue">You've done everything the school asked. You need to catch the head during school hours.</span>
			<br>
		<<elseif !Time.schoolDay>>
			<span class="blue">There's no service muster at the weekend.</span>
			<br>
		<<elseif Time.hour lt 9>>
			<span class="blue">The service muster isn't until nine.</span>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<span class="blue">You've missed today's service muster.</span>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

:: School Late Slip
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set $daily.school.lateSlip to 1>>
You are halfway down the corridor before you remember the rule.
<br><br>
You have been late often enough that no teacher will let you into a lesson without a slip from the head.
Before you can go to class, you have to report to Leighton's office and get one.
<br><br>
You turn around, walk back past the stairs, and open the office door.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Late Slip 2]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Late Slip 2
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>><<npc Leighton>><<person1>>
Leighton sits behind <<his>> desk with a pad of late slips in front of <<him>>.
<<He>> keeps looking at the paperwork on <<his>> desk as you approach.
<br><br>
"Name and lesson," <<he>> says, pushing the pad closer.
<br><br>
<<if $delinquency gte 700>>
	You start to answer, but <<he>> begins writing before you finish.
	"I've filled out enough of these for you to remember most of it."
<<elseif $delinquency gte 500>>
	<<He>> looks at the clock before writing your name on the slip.
	"Third time in two weeks, isn't it?"
<<else>>
	<<He>> writes your name and lesson on the slip, then tears it from the pad.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $delinquency gte 700>>
	Leighton finishes writing and puts the pen down.
	"If you keep arriving late, I won't keep giving you slips. I'll start sending letters home instead."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<He>> holds the slip towards you. When you take it, <<he>> keeps hold of the other end for a second.
"You need this before your teacher will let you into the lesson.
Next time, leave enough time to get here before class starts."<<stress 3>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
<<He>> releases the slip, leaving it in your hand.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Late Slip Go]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Late Slip Go
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<endevent>>
<<if ["Science Classroom", "Maths Classroom", "Housekeeping Classroom", "English Classroom", "History Classroom", "School Pool Entrance"].includes($schoolLateSlipTarget)>>
	<<set _target to $schoolLateSlipTarget>>
<<else>>
	<<set _target to "Hallways">>
<</if>>
<<unset $schoolLateSlipTarget>>
You take the slip and head for the lesson.
<br><br>
<<link "Next" _target>><<set $justEntered to true>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Suspension Notice
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<npc Leighton>><<person1>>
<<run schoolSuspensionBegin()>>
Leighton is waiting for you in the corridor. <<He>> does not have <<his>> usual detention pad with <<him>>.
<br><br>
"My office. Now."
<br><br>
You follow <<him>> inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Suspension Notice 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Suspension Notice 2
<<effects>>
Leighton sits behind the desk and opens a file filled with reports about your behaviour at school.
<<He>> turns the file towards you so you can see them.
"I chose not to punish you more seriously for these incidents... And that ends today."
<br><br>
<<if $schoolDiscipline.suspensions is 1>>
	<<He>> glares at you. "<span class="red">You're suspended for <<print $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft>> school days</span>, starting today."
<<else>>
	<<He>> glares at you. "<span class="red">You're suspended again</span>. This time, it's <<print $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft>> school days.
	Your last suspension clearly wasn't enough to stop this behaviour."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You stay in front of the desk, waiting while Leighton reaches into a drawer and takes out another sheet.
"Don't treat the suspension as time off.
You still have to report to the front gate at nine every school day during your suspension."
<br><br>
<<He>> places the second sheet beside the file.
"The council has arranged community service for you. You must complete <<print $schoolDiscipline.serviceRequired>> sessions.
Miss a required session, and your punishment will be extended."
<br><br>
Leighton signs the sheet and pushes it across the desk towards you.
"Now leave the school grounds."
<<stress 12>><<ggstress>><<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|School Gate Exit]]>><<endevent>><<schoolclothesreset>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Warning
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<npc Leighton>><<person1>>
<<run ensureSchoolDiscipline()>>
<<set $schoolDiscipline.notice to "">>
Leighton is waiting by the school gate when you arrive, holding a clipboard against <<his>> chest.
<br><br>
<<He>> speaks as soon as <<he>> sees you. "You've missed <<print $schoolDiscipline.serviceMissed>> community service sessions."
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	You start to explain yourself, but <<he>> raises a hand before you get far. You stop speaking.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	You lower your eyes. Leighton waits until you look back at <<him>> before continuing.
<<else>>
	You stay quiet. Leighton gives you a few seconds to answer, then continues.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"I need you to understand what happens if you keep missing them," <<he>> says.
"Community service is your last chance to deal with this through the school. If you keep skipping it,
I'll have to report it to the governors. After that, I won't be the one deciding what happens to you."
<br><br>
<<He>> lowers the clipboard and checks the page.
<br><br>
"You still <span class="red">have <<print Math.max($schoolDiscipline.serviceRequired - $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone, 0)>> sessions left to complete</span>. Start today."
<<stress 8>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Front Courtyard]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Absconded
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<npc Leighton>><<person1>><<run ensureSchoolDiscipline()>>
<<set $schoolDiscipline.notice to "">>
Leighton is waiting just inside the school gate with a sheet of paper in <<his>> hand. When you get closer,
<<he>> raises it so you can see your name.
<br><br>
"The supervisor sent this to me last night," <<he>> says. "It says you left before finishing your work yesterday."
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	You tell <<him>> the work was pointless and you were wasting your time there.
	Leighton waits until you finish before answering. "You were still supposed to stay until the session was over."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	You start to apologise, but Leighton stops you before you finish.
	"I don't need an apology. You still owe the time you missed."
<<else>>
	You stay quiet instead of making an excuse. Leighton watches you for a second, then lowers the paper.
	"At least you're not going to pretend it didn't happen."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Service Absconded 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Absconded 2
<<effects>>
"The supervisor could have refused to let you come back," Leighton says. "I spoke to <<him>>,
and <<he>> agreed to give you another chance."
<br><br>
Leighton folds the paper and puts it in <<his>> pocket.
<br><br>
"If you leave early again, I won't ask <<him>> to take you back."<<detention 2>><<stress 12>><<ggstress>><<gdelinquency>>
<br><br>
<span class="purple">The session you left early has been added back to the work you still need to complete</span>.
You have also received one extra session for leaving.
<<set _serviceOwed to schoolServiceAbscondPenalty()>>
<br><br>
You still <span class="red">have <<print _serviceOwed>> session<<if _serviceOwed isnot 1>>s<</if>> left to complete</span>.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Front Courtyard]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Readmission
<<autism-burnout-line "social">>
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<npc Leighton>><<person1>>
<<set _missed to $schoolDiscipline.serviceMissed>>
<<run schoolReadmit()>>
Leighton looks over the record of your community service,
checking each completed session before placing the sheet on <<his>> desk.
<<if _missed is 0>>
	"You attended every session and completed all of them. I was expecting to have to extend your punishment."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> slides your timetable across the desk towards you. "You can return to lessons from today. Try not to give me another reason to suspend you."
<<else>>
	<br><br>
	"You missed <<print _missed>> <<if _missed is 1>>session<<else>>sessions<</if>>, and someone had to remind you to attend," <<he>> says,
	looking over the sheet again. "Still, you've completed everything required."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> slides your timetable across the desk towards you. "You can return to lessons. I would prefer not to suspend you again."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<span class="green">Your suspension has ended.</span> You can attend lessons again.
<<stress -12>><<lllstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Report
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run ensureSchoolDiscipline()>>
<<generate1>><<person1>>

A council van is parked outside the school gate. A <<person>> wearing a bright safety jacket
stands beside it with a list of names.
<br><br>
<<He>> checks the list, finds your name, then marks it with a pen.
"Right. You're with me until eleven."
<br><br>
<<if $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone is 0>>
	<<He>> hands you a safety jacket several sizes too big and a worn pair of work gloves.
	"Rules are simple. Do the work and I sign off your hours. Leave before we're finished and I don't."
<<elseif $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone gte $schoolDiscipline.serviceRequired - 1>>
	<<He>> checks the list again.
	"Last one, isn't it? Finish this properly and you're done."
<<else>>
	<<He>> takes a safety jacket from the van and hands it to you.
	"Same one as last time," <<he>> says.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Service Report 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Report 2
<<effects>>
<<set $phase to random(1, 3)>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	You climb into the van with the other workers. It takes you to the park, where litter has been left across the grass behind the fountain.
	<br><br>
	The <<person>> gives you a rubbish bag and a litter picker, then points towards the grass.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	The van takes you to the high street. Someone has covered part of a wall with graffiti.
	The <<person>> hands you a bucket and a wire brush.
	<br><br>
	"Start there," <<he>> says, pointing to the nearest section of paint.
<<else>>
	Instead of getting into the van, the <<person>> leads you back through the school gate.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> takes you to a corridor, puts a mop and bucket in front of you, then points down the floor.
	"Start here. Do the whole corridor."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Get to work (2:00)|School Service Work]]>><<pass 120>><</link>>
<br>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 400>>
<<link [[Slip away while <<hes>> not looking|School Service Slip Away]]>><<pass 5>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
<br>
<<link [[Put the jacket down and walk off|School Service Walk Off]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Slip Away
<<set $outside to $phase is 3 ? 0 : 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<skulduggerycheck>>
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	You wait until the <<person>> turns away and starts moving things around in the back of the van.
	While <<he>> is busy, you walk away without saying anything.<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	You continue down the road without rushing. When you finally look back, the van is too far away for you to see.
	The <<person>> did not notice you leave, so <<he>> does not stop you or mark the session as completed.
	<br><br>
	<<run schoolServiceSlipAway()>>
	<<set _serviceExit to $phase is 1 ? "Park" : ($phase is 2 ? "High Street" : "Oxford Street")>>
	<<link [[Leave|_serviceExit]]>><<endevent>><<schoolclothesreset>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You wait until the <<person>> turns towards the back of the van, then start walking away.
	<br><br>
	You only make it a short distance before <<he>> notices. "Where do you think you're going?"
	<br><br>
	You stop and look back. The <<person>> remains beside the van, watching to see what you do next.
	You can return and finish the work, or keep walking and leave the session early.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Keep walking|School Service Walk Off]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go back and work|School Service Work]]>><<pass 120>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: School Service Walk Off
<<set $outside to $phase is 3 ? 0 : 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run schoolServiceAbscond()>>
You take off the safety jacket, leave it on the bench, and walk away from the work session.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
The <<person>> watches you leave. <<He>> does not try to stop you. Instead,
<<he>> takes a pen from <<his>> pocket and marks your name on the attendance sheet.
<br><br>
"Fine," <<he>> calls after you. "<span class="red">I'll report that you left early</span>."
<<ggdelinquency>><<delinquency 3>>
<br><br>
<<set _serviceExit to $phase is 1 ? "Park" : ($phase is 2 ? "High Street" : "Oxford Street")>>
<<link [[Leave|_serviceExit]]>><<endevent>><<schoolclothesreset>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Service Work
<<set $outside to $phase is 3 ? 0 : 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<autism-burnout-line "work">>
<<autism-service "School Service Work">>
<<if !_autismServiceFired>>
	<<if $phase is 1>>
		You walk along the grass with a litter picker in one hand and a rubbish sack in the other.
		Before long, the sack starts pulling heavily against your arm.
		<br><br>
		You pick up bottles, wrappers, empty cans, and even an old shoe.
		Students and other people pass along the nearby path while you work.
		Some glance at you as they go, making it obvious that they know why you are here.<<status -10>><<llcool>>
		<br><br>
		<<if $exhibitionism gte 35>>
			Instead of hiding from the attention,
			you find yourself standing a little straighter whenever someone looks your way.<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
		<<else>>
			You keep your eyes on the ground and focus on filling the sack, trying not to notice who is watching you.
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<</if>>
		<<tiredness 8>><<gtiredness>>
	<<elseif $phase is 2>>
		You spend the morning removing paint from a wall. You press the tool against one small section at a time,
		rubbing until the paint finally starts to come away.
		<br><br>
		Your shoulders begin to ache, but there is still plenty left to clean.
		<br><br>
		<<if $schoolDiscipline.serviceDone gte 3>>
			You have done this enough times to know what works.
			You start at the top and clean one small area before moving to the next, finishing each section before going lower.
		<<else>>
			Some of the paint spreads across the wall instead of coming off.
			The <<person>> points out the marks and makes you clean those areas again.
		<</if>>
		<<tiredness 10>><<stress 6>><<gtiredness>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>
		Two students from your year walk past on the other side of the road.
		One says something to the other while looking towards you, and they both laugh before continuing on.
		<<status -10>><<llcool>>
	<<else>>
		You spend the next two hours cleaning the school corridors.
		You mop the science block from one end to the other, then clean the stairs.
		<br><br>
		When you return, the <<person>> points out several marks left on the floor,
		so you have to mop part of the corridor again.
		<br><br>
		<<if $schoolstate is "lunch" or $schoolstate is "third">>
			The school bell rings. A few moments later, students begin filling the corridor.
			<br><br>
			You move against the wall and hold the mop close to yourself so people can pass.
			Several students look at you while they walk by,
			and you have to stand there until the corridor is clear enough to continue.
			<<stress 8>><<gstress>><<status -10>><<llcool>>
		<<else>>
			Very few people pass through this part of the school.
			Without anyone watching you, the work feels easier to get through.
			<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|School Service Work 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: School Service Work 2
<<effects>><<set _last to schoolServiceComplete()>>
When done, the <<person>> takes your sheet and signs it after checking that your work is finished.
<span class="green">One session down.</span>
<br><br>
<<if _last>>
	<<if $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft gt 0>>
		"That's your lot," <<he>> says, tucking the clipboard under <<his>> arm.
		"School still won't have you back for another <<print $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft>> day<<if $schoolDiscipline.daysLeft isnot 1>>s<</if>>, mind.
		That part's not mine."
		<<else>>
		"That's your lot," <<he>> says, tucking the clipboard under <<his>> arm. "Go and get yourself signed back in."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|School Front Courtyard]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Duty Cleaning
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set $daily.school.detentionAttended to 1>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	The changing rooms are filthy after a swimming lesson. Wet footprints cover the floor,
	the benches are covered in water, and Leighton leaves you to clean all of it.
	<br><br>
	You rinse the mop until the water runs clearer, then wipe down the benches before starting on the floor.
	Water from the mop splashes onto the benches again, forcing you to wipe them a second time.
	<br><br>
	Someone has also left a wet sock beneath one of the benches. You try to ignore it,
	but eventually pick it up and throw it away with the rest of the rubbish.
	<<tiredness 8>><<gtiredness>>
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	"Clean under the desks as well," Leighton tells you before leaving.
	<br><br>
	You spend the next forty minutes kneeling beside each desk in an empty classroom.
	Old chewing gum has been stuck underneath many of them, so you use a plastic scraper to remove it piece by piece.
	<br><br>
	<<if $exhibitionism gte 35 and $worn.lower.type.includes("skirt")>>
		Working on the floor in a skirt makes the position awkward.
		You keep adjusting your clothes as you move from one desk to the next, but nobody enters the classroom.
		<<arousal 200>><<garousal>>
	<<else>>
		Your knees begin to hurt before you reach the last row.
		The edge of the plastic scraper wears down as you work, but several desks still have gum stuck beneath them.
	<</if>>
	<<tiredness 8>><<gtiredness>>
<<else>>
	Leighton makes you empty every bin in the ground-floor classrooms and carry the rubbish outside to the yard.
	<br><br>
	There is a trolley nearby, but Leighton tells you that only staff are allowed to use it.
	You have to carry the bags out by hand, making several trips between the classrooms and the yard.
	<br><br>
	By the fourth trip, the smell bothers you less than having to walk past the unused trolley again.
	<<tiredness 10>><<gtiredness>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|School Duty Cleaning 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Duty Cleaning 2
<<effects>>
When you finish, Leighton returns to inspect your work. <<He>> walks through the area slowly,
checking what you cleaned before coming back to you.
<br><br>
<<if $delinquency gte 700>>
	"Better," <<he>> says. "You've had plenty of practice."
<<else>>
	"It'll do," <<he>> says. "You can always come back tomorrow if you enjoyed it."
<</if>>
<<stress 6>><<gstress>><<delinquency -3>><<lldelinquency>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
